      "content": "The sudden spikes you're experiencing could be caused by an overpopulation of a dominant species, often Acetobacter or Gluconobacter, which can thrive in the presence of excess lactic acid. When these species become dominant, they can produce acetic acid more forcefully, causing a rapid shift in pH and resulting in the unbalanced, sour flavors you're describing. In such cases, the microbial community can become sentient, so to speak, with these dominant species dictating the landscape of your sourdough rather than a harmonious balance of yeast and bacteria.",
